\label{prop:stable-model}
If $V$ is a finite-dimensional left $A$-module and $\Lambda$ is an
$R$-order in $A$, then $V$ contains a full left $\Lambda$-lattice.

\label{thm:cm-dichotomy}
For a full lattice $L\subseteq\mathbb C$, either $O(L)=\mathbb Z$
or $O(L)$ is an order in an imaginary quadratic field.

Let \((C^\bullet,d)\) be a finite complex of finite-dimensional vector spaces and let \(T\) be a chain endomorphism. Then
\[
 \prod_i\det(I-tT_{C^i})^{(-1)^i}
   =\prod_i\det(I-tT_{H^i})^{(-1)^i}.
 \tag{Z4}\label{eq:cohomological-determinant}
\]

For the specified state, patch and gates,
\begin{equation}
 f_\theta(s)=\left(\prod_{i=0}^3s_i\right)
              \left(\prod_{i=0}^3\cos\theta_i\right).
 \label{eq:qnn-exact-output}
\end{equation}

